<title>MEXICO: Disgruntled Mexican shoots soothsayer.</title>
<headline>Disgruntled Mexican shoots soothsayer.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Mexican man apparently disgruntled at the results of a Tarot card reading pulled out a gun and shot a woman soothsayer twice in the head, police said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Tarot card reader Gloria Garza Villanueva, 40, survived the attack but was in serious condition in hospital, state judicial police spokesman Antonio Lopez told Reuters in the northern city of Monterrey.</p>
<p>The whereabouts of the assailant were unknown, Lopez said, adding police were going over Garza's client list with the hope of tracking him down.</p>
